{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>You have seen</b> — in Your wisdom, for You behold without doubt the trouble and vexation that the wicked man does, for it is in Your hand to give him retribution at any time You desire." "<b>Upon You he casts his care</b> — like 'for his care, this vexation,' for he saw that many times You helped the orphan who has none to help him. And Rabbi Judah ben Balaam said: Because You behold the trouble and vexation, You give him his every desire; therefore the poor man forsakes to lean [on You] — and behold, the end of the verse will prove him false."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {1 "The reading לסמוך ('to lean') is taken as given; Ibn Ezra's terseness leaves the subject of יעזוב ambiguous, and ben Balaam's reading is rendered hyper-literally as transmitted."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:58.782993657Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}